This script automatically retrieves and plots the 2D cross-sectional shape of an airfoil using data from the UIUC Airfoil Data Site. The program uses the requests library to fetch a text file containing the exact physical coordinates for a specified airfoil design, such as the mh70. It then cleans and parses those coordinates, discarding invalid lines, before using Matplotlib to draw the precise curve of the airfoil on a graph.
